== Special Balls ==
Special Balls have a unique passive ability and can be level up and combined with other special balls during each run. Some Special Balls are unlocked by default, while others require reaching specific stages to unlock. They can be leveled up to level 3 in each run, improving their damage and abilities.


To better understand abilitiy triggering rules, refer to the table below:

{| class="wikitable"
|+ How to trigger abilities?
|-
! Ablility Types !! Abilities !! Triggers
|-
| On-Hit Effects || Destroy, Pass Through, AOE, Spawn|| On-Hit only
|-
| Status Effects || Poison, Burn, Freeze etc. || On-Hit, On-Damage, On-Timer, On-Shoot, Spawn
|-
|}


A ball's abilities consist of three aspects:

On-Hit Effects: can be triggered by hit only. On-Hit Effects include Destroy, Pass through, AOE, and Spawn. 

Status Triggers: the abilities to trigger Statues Effects. Status Triggers include On-Hit, AOE, On-Timer, On-Shoot, Spawn.

Status Effects: can be triggerd by hit, AOE, Timer, Shoot, and Spawn. Status Effects include Instant Death(from black hole), Poison, Burn, Freeze etc..


There are 4 types of On-Hit Effects:

Pass Through: Balls pass thourgh the target, ideal for hitting multiple targets.

Destroy: Balls destroy after hit. Though regarded as the least‑favoured type, these balls are usually having powerful abilities. Note: fusing two Destroy balls may lose one of their abililies.

AOE: Radiation from Nuclear Bomb, etc..

Spawn: Spawn Clones, Baby balls or Summons.


There are 5 Status Triggers:

On-Hit: when balls hit target. 

AOE: when balls deal damage. Note: Radiation from Nuclear Bomb counts as AOE, thus can trigger Status Effect.

On-Timer: Trigger at fixed time-intervals.

On-Shoot: when balls "shoot". Spawned balls don't count as "shoot".

Spawn: Spawn Clones, Baby balls or Summons. Spawns can provide bonus triggers. 


There are 3 types of Special Balls: '''Base Balls''', '''Fused Balls''' and '''Evolved Balls.'''

=== Base Balls ===
Base Balls are Special Balls that can be offered to you when you level up during a run, as long as you have them unlocked. There are a total of 21 Base Balls in the game currently, and every character has an assigned Base Ball that they start the run with. Certain base balls are unavailable at the start of the game and can only be unlocked for use by completing certain [[levels|pit levels]].
