=== Fused Balls ===
{{main|Fusion Mechanics}}

Before fusing balls, take this into account:
{| class="wikitable"
|+ General Rules for Abilities
|-
! Aspect !! Ability Type
|-
| On-Hit Effects || Pass Through/Destroy, AOE, Spawn
|-
| Status Triggers || On-Hit,AOE, On-Timer, On-Shoot, Spawn
|-
| Status Effect || Instant kill, Bleeding, etc.
|}

Spawn is arguably the best ability. It can compensate Destroy effect. For example, Cell(Clone) x Bomb(Destroy) is an "indestructible" bomb, since the bomb is cloned and destroyed at the same time.

Full Screen Trigger is the best option to trigger Status Effect. 

[[File:BleedXFreeze.png|thumb|alt=Fusion Ball Example (BleedXFreeze)|470x470px|Example for fusing Bleed and Freeze Balls]]
Fused Balls are balls that are created by fusing 2 other ''"unfused"'' level 3 Special Balls together using the [[Fusion Reactor|'''Fusion Reactor''']]. You can fuse 2 Base Balls, 2 Evolved Balls or even 1 Base Ball and 1 Evolved Ball together. However, the same ball cannot be fused with itself, and if 2 balls can otherwise combine into an Evolved Ball, then you '''can't fuse them''' and can only evolve them instead (although this does not apply for pairs of Special Balls whose only common evolution requires 3 or more Special Balls at the same time, such as {{il|Nosferatu}} or {{il|Elemental}}). As a result, there are <code>(90*89) {Special Ball Combos} - 89 {Evolution Combos} = 7921</code> potential functionally different fused balls.

Fused Balls will have the name and effects of their fused balls combined, and their icon will also be updated to match the fusion. For example, fusing '''Bleed''' and '''Freeze''' will result in '''Bleed X Freeze''', which has both abilities from '''Bleed''' and '''Freeze'''. The priority of which effects and stats are combined are dependent on the component balls involved. Additionally, unlike with evolved balls, while '''the order of the fused balls does not change the functional stats/abilities of the resulting ball''', its name will be different and its appearance ''may'' be different depending on the specific balls fused (e.g. '''Egg Sac X Poison''' looks the same as '''Poison X Egg Sac''', however '''Spider Queen X Vampire Lord''' has a completely different sprite from '''Vampire Lord X Spider Queen'''). Note that the only way to change the order of fused balls is to change the order in which they're acquired, and one cannot manually select the order of balls for fusion at this time,
